cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use xingo-extprec, please cite it using these metadata. Each release is archived on Zenodo with its own DOI."
# TODO(owner): add `doi:` and `identifiers:` (concept DOI and version DOI) once Zenodo has archived the first release, as in xingo-sparse.
type: software
title: "xingo-extprec: extended precision and rigorous enclosures for numerical linear algebra"
abstract: "Extended precision for numerical linear algebra in pure Rust: double-double arithmetic whose operations and elementary functions have proven error bounds, compensated sums and dot products with SIMD kernels that return the scalar results bit for bit, outward-rounded interval arithmetic without changing the rounding mode, and rigorous enclosures of sparse residuals with iterative-refinement polishing. The extended-precision layer of the Xingó solver."
authors:
  - family-names: Leite
    given-names: André
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/StrategicProjects/xingo-extprec"
url: "https://strategicprojects.github.io/xingo-extprec/"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-18
keywords:
  - double-double arithmetic
  - extended precision
  - error-free transformations
  - interval arithmetic
  - verified computing
  - compensated summation
  - elementary functions
  - iterative refinement
  - Rust
